WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.044 --> 00:00:01.809
(band stops playing)
(audience cheers)

00:00:01.809 --> 00:00:04.320
- Welcome back, I'm here, with
Cedric the Entertainer and

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.406
Pam Grier and also Veda Tunstall

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.699
from the documentary "Descending", here.

00:00:08.699 --> 00:00:09.880
And one of the producers
with her, Quest Love,

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.150
dialed in from New York.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.880
And joining us now from Atlanta
is the youngest daughter

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.570
of Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.
She's an attorney and activist

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.880
and author and the CEO of the King Center.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.200
She's got a lot of jobs.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.743
Let's say hi to Dr. Bernice King, y'all.

00:00:24.743 --> 00:00:27.473
(audience cheering)

00:00:27.473 --> 00:00:28.306
- Hello.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.373
- Hello. Say hello to everyone.

00:00:33.627 --> 00:00:36.208
- Hello, everybody. Good to be here.

00:00:36.208 --> 00:00:37.460
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:38.643
- It's a,
- What's up!

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.240
- He's like, "I got a shout out."

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.030
It's so lovely to have you
here. We were just talking

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.160
about Questlove's new
documentary, "Descendant".

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.230
Your father frequently connected the past

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.700
to the present in his speeches.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.580
So what do you think his
purpose in doing that was?

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.470
- I think it was a few things.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.610
One, it was an effort, one, to help

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.410
inform the present to help

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.490
guide us in the present and future.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:08.250
And also to help us to correct some things

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.660
in the present and in the future.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.360
And help people to understand that

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.340
everybody's history is different.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.820
And oftentimes we make assumptions.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.400
And if we don't understand the history

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.200
and that's the good, the bad, indifferent

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.570
we will bring certain
beliefs to a situation.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:31.710
And so to dispel a lot of
things, myths, some half truths

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:35.904
he found it necessary to
really give the global context

00:01:35.904 --> 00:01:38.100
of the, of the experience
of African Americans,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.590
in particular in this nation.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:44.400
And also to help the people who were

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.580
in that movement understand
that this may have

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.130
been the circumstance that we were brought

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.940
to this nation, under
this depersonalization.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.430
But we are in a movement
now where I'm gonna help to

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.580
boost your personalization,
help you to understand

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:03.270
that you are somebody,
you often reminded us

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:05.760
that in spite of what
happened, we are somebody.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.440
And that boosted them around strength

00:02:08.842 --> 00:02:10.262
(audience cheering)
and the hope of the faith

00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:12.600
that they needed, in spite of injustices

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.010
that we were faced with.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:16.680
- Absolutely. Well, you were so young

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:20.010
When your father passed. What
memories do you have of him?

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.370
- Yeah, you know, I tell
people, unfortunately,

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.470
I only have one but it's
a special one because

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:28.050
it's the only one that I
shared with him, that none of

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:31.320
the other siblings shared.
And that was a little game

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.530
that we played when he would
come home and I would run up

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.600
into his arms and he said,
"We're gonna play the kissing

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.650
game today." And essentially
what that was is each one

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.720
of us had a spot on his face.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.180
My brother's on either
side of the cheek, I was

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.990
on the forehead, my sister was
off to the side of the mouth.

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:51.450
And my mom, of course, smacked
bed in the middle there.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:55.080
And he would say, "Okay, where is"

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.760
and he would just call everybody's name.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.867
My nickname was Bunny,
like the bunny rabbit,

00:02:58.867 --> 00:03:01.710
"Where's Bunny kissing
me?", I would hit him there.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.710
And he actually would call
them sugar spots, you know

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.140
in the black community we
called them, "gimme some sugar".

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.020
So I gave him some sugar
on each one of those spots,

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.640
he called each person's name.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.790
And that was our little bonding experience

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:19.710
because when I was born, he
started traveling even more.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.480
And so he wasn't as home as much.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:26.020
And I think he felt that he
needed to do something special,

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:29.820
so that I would have
that connection with him

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:33.870
because my father always had
a sense that he was not gonna

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:37.290
live a long life and so
he wanted to make sure

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:40.830
that there were meaningful
moments with each one of us.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.655
- Well, that's a beautiful memory.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.880
(audience cheering)

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.440
We wanna hear how you're being

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.110
of service this Martin Luther
King Jr Day, everybody.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:51.840
So tell us on Instagram, just tag the show

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:52.860
and we will be right back

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:55.260
with "What I'm Liking",
other than this episode.

